cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use MagnetronLab or its experimental dataset in teaching or research, please cite it as below."
title: "MagnetronLab: Interactive 3D Virtual Lab and Non-Ideal Physics Simulator for the Cylindrical Magnetron e/m Experiment"
type: software
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-11-25"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - physics-education
  - magnetron-cutoff
  - charge-to-mass-ratio
  - vacuum-diode
  - particle-simulation
  - webgl
  - threejs
authors:
  - family-names: "MagnetronLab"
    given-names: "Author"
    alias: "Please replace with your name before publishing"
abstract: >-
  An open-source 3D virtual laboratory and C++17 particle-dynamics simulator for
  the cylindrical vacuum-diode magnetron cutoff (Hull method) e/m experiment.
  Combines real dual-channel experimental measurements (central anode and guard
  rings) with a five-layer non-ideal physical model covering filament potential
  gradient, thermionic emission velocity, magnetic-field tilt, filament end
  cooling, and finite open-shell Laplace fringing fields.
